# Branding admin — "Promote to Prod"
#
# Shared secret the promote-receive function checks before writing anything.
# Same value in BOTH places: your local .env AND the production site's
# environment variables (Netlify dashboard > Project configuration >
# Environment variables). Generate one with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
PROMOTE_SECRET=

# Only set this locally (in your own .env, never in the production site's
# env vars). It's how your local admin-promote function knows where "prod"
# is. Prod has nowhere further to promote to, so it should NOT have this
# set — leaving it unset there is what makes the promote button correctly
# report "not configured" if someone clicks it on the live site.
PROD_SITE_URL=https://your-site-name.netlify.app
